    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0723" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg603"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Japanese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 207.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 32, of the 28th ultimo, requesting the good offices of the
                    Government of the United States in securing the release of three Japanese
                    merchants, Messrs. Nobe Ichitaro, Yagabe Chiuzaburo, and his son Gyo, who were
                    captured by Russian soldiers while traveling in Korea on commercial business and
                    held as prisoners of war; and to inform you that on the 30th ultimo I had the
                    pleasure of instructing Ambassador Meyer to use his good offices with the
                    Russian Government for the release of the three Japanese merchants mentioned, in
                    accordance with your request.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
